{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.MassCoefficientShadowPrice","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.MassCoefficientShadowPrice","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Units.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Invertible.Defs"],"declarations":19,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MassCoefficientShadowPrice.weight_ne_zero_of_shadow_price_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MassCoefficientShadowPrice.weight_ne_zero_of_shadow_price_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-coefficient-shadow-price.lean#L156-L164","doc":"Contrapositive, which is how a search uses it: a block that prices anything\nat all must have a nonzero canonical weight — so under convention D it must have\nat most two rows. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MassCoefficientShadowPrice.shadow_price_eq_zero_of_weight_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MassCoefficientShadowPrice.shadow_price_eq_zero_of_weight_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-coefficient-shadow-price.lean#L145-L154","doc":"**And therefore kills the shadow price**, whatever the scaling function\ndoes. So a block the row cap annihilates contributes nothing to\n`B = (Σ_λ C_λ · S_λ) · m_e` — no `S_λ` can rescue it, because the vanishing is\nupstream of the nuclear datum. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MassCoefficientShadowPrice.coefficient_eq_zero_of_weight_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MassCoefficientShadowPrice.coefficient_eq_zero_of_weight_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-coefficient-shadow-price.lean#L128-L143","doc":"**A vanishing Wedderburn weight kills the coefficient.** Immediate from\n`C_eq`, and the reason it matters is that convention D's row cap\n(`QOU/Hecke/RowCap.lean`: a column of height `≥ 3` has no injective filling into\na 2-dimensional fibre) makes `tilde w_λ = 0` for every `ℓ(λ) > 2`. Those blocks\ntherefore price nothing — which is the step `qou-a5jk` left open and\n`qou-8na1` had already observed as an instance (`C_[1,1,1] = w̃·h/2 = 0` makes\n`uStar = C·S = 0` consistent rather than contradictory).\n\nThe implication is proved here; the antecedent is the corpus's, cited not\nre-derived. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MassCoefficientShadowPrice.coefficient_nuclear_independent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MassCoefficientShadowPrice.coefficient_nuclear_independent","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-coefficient-shadow-price.lean#L117-L126","doc":"The coefficient `C_λ` is independent of the nuclear datum: cancelling the\nscaling off the shadow price recovers the partition-only `C_λ`.  The\ninvertibility of `S_λ` — over a field, the old `S_λ ≠ 0` — is supplied by\nthe unit `s` with `S_λ = ↑s`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MassCoefficientShadowPrice.normalization","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MassCoefficientShadowPrice.normalization","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-coefficient-shadow-price.lean#L108-L115","doc":"At the normalisation point `S_λ = 1`, the shadow price equals the\npartition-only coefficient `C_λ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MassCoefficientShadowPrice.shadow_price_weight_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MassCoefficientShadowPrice.shadow_price_weight_form","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-coefficient-shadow-price.lean#L99-L106","doc":"The shadow price in canonical-weight form:\n`u_λ* = tilde w_λ · (h·⅟2) · S_λ`.  Combines the strong-duality\nfactorisation with the LP scaling identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MassCoefficientShadowPrice.factor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MassCoefficientShadowPrice.factor","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-coefficient-shadow-price.lean#L97-L97","doc":"Strong-duality factorisation `u_λ* = C_λ · S_λ`\n(`prop:operator-selection-lp`: strong duality + complementary slackness). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MassCoefficientShadowPrice.C_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MassCoefficientShadowPrice.C_eq","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-coefficient-shadow-price.lean#L94-L94","doc":"LP shadow-price scaling identity `C_λ = tilde w_λ · h·⅟2` (definitional;\nthe same `C_λ` as `prop:wedderburn-weight-canonical`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MassCoefficientShadowPrice.uStar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MassCoefficientShadowPrice.uStar","kind":"def","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-coefficient-shadow-price.lean#L91-L91","doc":"Optimal dual variable (shadow price) of the `λ`-Frobenius constraint. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MassCoefficientShadowPrice.S","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MassCoefficientShadowPrice.S","kind":"def","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-coefficient-shadow-price.lean#L89-L89","doc":"Scaling function `S_λ(Z,N,A)` — the only nuclear-datum-dependent factor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MassCoefficientShadowPrice.C","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MassCoefficientShadowPrice.C","kind":"def","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-coefficient-shadow-price.lean#L87-L87","doc":"LP shadow-price coefficient `C_λ` (partition-only, no nuclear datum). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MassCoefficientShadowPrice.contentSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MassCoefficientShadowPrice.contentSum","kind":"def","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-coefficient-shadow-price.lean#L85-L85","doc":"Content sum `c(λ) = Σ (j - i)` — determines the scaling type\n(`>0` volume, `=0` isospin, `<0` charge). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MassCoefficientShadowPrice.w","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MassCoefficientShadowPrice.w","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-coefficient-shadow-price.lean#L82-L82","doc":"Canonical q-deformed Wedderburn weight `tilde w_λ`\n(cf. `WedderburnWeightCanonical`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MassCoefficientShadowPrice.h","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MassCoefficientShadowPrice.h","kind":"def","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-coefficient-shadow-price.lean#L79-L79","doc":"Hecke-generator scalar `h = q - q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MassCoefficientShadowPrice.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MassCoefficientShadowPrice.mk","kind":"ctor","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-coefficient-shadow-price.lean#L77-L77","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MassCoefficientShadowPrice","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MassCoefficientShadowPrice","kind":"class","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-coefficient-shadow-price.lean#L68-L97","doc":"The shadow-price discipline for the mass-formula coefficients, polymorphic\nin the ground ring `R` (with `2` invertible).\n\nAn instance records, for the nuclear operator-selection LP:\n  • the canonical Wedderburn weight `tilde w_λ` and the Hecke scalar `h`;\n  • the partition-only LP coefficient `C_λ = tilde w_λ · h·⅟2`;\n  • the nuclear-datum scaling function `S_λ(Z,N,A)`;\n  • the optimal dual variable `u_λ*` with the strong-duality factorisation\n    `u_λ* = C_λ · S_λ` (`prop:operator-selection-lp`). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:mass-coefficient-shadow-price","label":"prop:mass-coefficient-shadow-price","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-coefficient-shadow-price.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Partition.parts","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Partition.parts","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-coefficient-shadow-price.lean#L66-L66","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Partition.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Partition.mk","kind":"ctor","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-coefficient-shadow-price.lean#L65-L65","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Partition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Partition","kind":"structure","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-coefficient-shadow-price.lean#L63-L66","doc":"A partition `λ ⊢ k` (placeholder; an abstract index so the discipline holds\nfor any realisation). ","signatureChunk":0}]}